                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "GAME BEATTEN  (no soluce, 100% objects, 98% map, 92% orbs)\n\nWE LIKE\n\n- a metroidvania puzzle plateformer\n\n- a decent 8 bit pixel-art\n\n- the good OG melodies (musics and sounds are so inportant in a game)\n\n- the evolving abilities of the character\n\n- a lot to explore\n\n- some plateforme sections are a bit challenging\n\n- the infinite lifes, and you will need it\n\n- very worth it for 0,97 $\n\n\nTHE MEDIUM, THE BAD, AND THE UGGLY\n\n- the character is slow, but reading many comments i thought it will be worse\nIndeed, the gameplay will not please to everyone, at least during the first minutes :\nthere is a real latency to attack, and to jump, like some old plateformer games\n\n- mobs are easy, bosses are easy too\n\n- the map is hard to use, unclear (for example i noticed the (x ; y) coordinates of the character only during the last hour ...)\n\n- some PNJ give you confusing informations\n\n- not always fun : sometimes you don't know where to go next, so you walk around in the first levels again and again, at slug speed ... Some players will stop the game here\n\n- puzzles are not challenging enought, it's to bad because there was plenty to do with the combinations of the 3 abilities \n\n- some objects are useless in the game, and it's impossible to guess it ... So you feel betrayed because it cost you hours of exploration\n\n- 2 things to collect (objects and blue orbs) and most of blue orbs are almost useless too\n\n- so exploration is not rewarded enought, it s a big probleme in a metroidvania puzzle plateformer\n\n- a very very short end, not rewarded nether on that point after 20h of gameplay (without guide)\n\n\nFINAL SCORES :\n\n- for 9,75 $ :  12 / 20\n- for 0,97 $ :  14,5 / 20 \n- without price consideration :  13 / 20",
